   $q$A community theater sold 250 tickets for 1610 dollars. Adult tickets cost 8 dollars and student tickets cost 5 dollars, so $x + y = 250$ and $8x + 5y = 1610$. Which expression gives $\begin{bmatrix} x \\ y \end{bmatrix}$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix} 5 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 250 \\\\ 1610 \\end{bmatrix}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix} 5 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 250 \\\\ 1610 \\end{bmatrix}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-determinant"},{"text":"$\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 5 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 250 \\\\ 1610 \\end{bmatrix}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-by-matrix-instead-of-inverse"},{"text":"$-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 5 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 250 \\\\ 1610 \\end{bmatrix}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-swap-diagonal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-\frac{1}{3}\begin{bmatrix} 5 & -1 \\ -8 & 1 \end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix} 250 \\ 1610 \end{bmatrix}$$q$, $q$The coefficient matrix $\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 8 & 5 \end{bmatrix}$ has determinant $5 - 8 = -3$, so its inverse is $-\frac{1}{3}\begin{bmatrix} 5 & -1 \\ -8 & 1 \end{bmatrix}$, which gives 120 adult and 130 student tickets. The choice with $\frac{1}{3}$ computes the determinant as $8 - 5$ instead of $5 - 8$.$q$, 'draft', null)
